    "message": "fix(models.dev): let a model's own provider describe it\n\nThe last item left open by the reasoning arc. Model metadata -- vision\nsupport, context length, prices -- was matched against every provider's models\nflattened into one namespace, first writer wins, and the winner was decided by\nwhichever order models.dev happened to serialise its JSON.\n\nMeasured against the live 2026-08 index (193 providers): 3,757 model ids are\nclaimed by more than one provider, and 234 of those disagree about whether the\nmodel can read images. So a model could be told it was blind because an\nunrelated provider hosts something with the same name -- and vision routing\nthen diverts a request that never needed diverting.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. The model's own provider is consulted first, via the same alias map the\n   reasoning-capability lookup already uses (open_router -> openrouter,\n   fireworks -> fireworks-ai). The cross-provider index remains as a fallback,\n   because most of what a gateway resells is not published under that gateway.\n\n2. The fallback index now accumulates field by field instead of\n   first-writer-wins, so whether a field is populated at all no longer depends\n   on upstream serialisation order.\n\nBoth are merges rather than replacements. Choosing wholesale looked correct and\ncost 11 models metadata they have today, which is a regression however much\nmore authoritative the source is -- so per field, the model's own provider wins\nwhere it says anything, and a namesake elsewhere fills only the gaps.\n\nVerification\n------------\nAgainst the real 4.2 MB index, not a fixture:\n\n    model ids claimed by >1 provider     3,757\n      ...disagreeing about vision          234\n    models whose metadata changes        1,936\n    models that LOSE metadata                0\n\nGuards mutation-tested, each failing by name:\n\n    M1 scoping removed              -> models_own_provider_decides\n    M2 scoped chosen wholesale      -> sparse_provider_does_not_strip\n    M3 alias map ignored            -> provider_alias_map_is_used_for_scoping\n    M4 flat index back to first-wins-> sparse_provider_does_not_strip\n\nM3 survived a first pass: the test asserted an answer the flat fallback\nhappened to give anyway. It now uses a competing provider that answers\ndifferently and is reached first, so the alias is the only thing that can\nproduce the expected result.\n\nLocal CI: ruff format --check, ruff check, ty clean; pytest 4,840 passed with\nthe documented 6 test_install_ps1_* baseline failures.\n\nNot done\n--------\nTwo providers that both describe a model and disagree still resolve by\niteration order in the fallback, which only matters for a model whose own\nprovider says nothing about the field. Making that deterministic needs a rule\nfor which provider to believe, and there is no evidence yet for what that rule\nshould be.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
